From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:20:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "drm/msm/a6xx_gmu: erhai: retry the a8xx CM3 boot
 (100ms poll x4) to self-heal the intermittent FW_INIT_RESULT timeout"

This reverts commit ef4d9b41ae17.

The intermittent FW_INIT_RESULT timeouts the original retried followed from
the mis-sized device tree windows (the RSCC at gpu+0x50000 outside the GPU
node's 0x40000 kgsl_3d0_reg_memory window, and the GX GDSC left unbound by
9c9eefdef1 because the gxclkctl node mapped only 4 KiB), which kept a
wedged GMU from being power collapsed between boots; with the windows fixed
the single upstream 100 ms poll is used again.

Tested on a OnePlus Pad 3 (SM8750) with the whole series: the GPU
powers up at probe (no -19), the CX GDSC collapses on runtime suspend,
IGT msm_recovery gpu-fault recovers in 5 of 5 runs, and 2.5 h of desktop
use ran 3,227 runtime-PM cycles without a GMU wedge.

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 61 ++++++++++-----------------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 64e8d1ba8b8..d6400019d12 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -381,49 +381,34 @@ static int a6xx_gmu_start(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu = container_of(gmu, struct a6xx_gpu, gmu);
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = &a6xx_gpu->base;
 	u32 mask, reset_val, val;
-	int ret, i;
-
-	for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
-		val = gmu_read(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_DTCM_START + 0xff8);
-		if (val <= 0x20010004) {
-			mask = 0xffffffff;
-			reset_val = 0xbabeface;
-		} else {
-			mask = 0x1ff;
-			reset_val = 0x100;
-		}
+	int ret;
+
+	val = gmu_read(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_DTCM_START + 0xff8);
+	if (val <= 0x20010004) {
+		mask = 0xffffffff;
+		reset_val = 0xbabeface;
+	} else {
+		mask = 0x1ff;
+		reset_val = 0x100;
+	}
 
-		gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 1);
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 1);
 
-		/* Set the log wptr index
-		 * note: downstream saves the value in poweroff and restores it here
-		 */
-		if (adreno_is_a8xx(adreno_gpu))
-			gmu_write(gmu, REG_A8XX_GMU_GENERAL_9, 0);
-		else if (adreno_is_a7xx(adreno_gpu))
-			gmu_write(gmu, REG_A7XX_GMU_GENERAL_9, 0);
-		else
-			gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GPU_GMU_CX_GMU_PWR_COL_CP_RESP, 0);
+	/* Set the log wptr index
+	 * note: downstream saves the value in poweroff and restores it here
+	 */
+	if (adreno_is_a8xx(adreno_gpu))
+		gmu_write(gmu, REG_A8XX_GMU_GENERAL_9, 0);
+	else if (adreno_is_a7xx(adreno_gpu))
+		gmu_write(gmu, REG_A7XX_GMU_GENERAL_9, 0);
+	else
+		gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GPU_GMU_CX_GMU_PWR_COL_CP_RESP, 0);
 
-		gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 0);
 
-		/*
-		 * erhai: the a8xx CM3 boot intermittently misses the 10 ms
-		 * FW_INIT_RESULT window (=> "GMU firmware initialization timed
-		 * out" -> OOB GPU_SET storm -> hangcheck -> frozen display; seen
-		 * on #82/#83/#84 even with the cold-boot reload). Lengthen the
-		 * poll to 100 ms and retry the CM3 boot up to 4 times before
-		 * giving up, so a slow/glitchy boot self-heals instead of
-		 * wedging the GPU irrecoverably ("cx gdsc didn't collapse").
-		 */
-		ret = gmu_poll_timeout(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT,
-			val, (val & mask) == reset_val, 100, 100000);
-		if (!ret)
-			break;
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 0);
 
-		DRM_DEV_ERROR(gmu->dev,
-			"erhai: GMU boot attempt %d/4 timed out, retrying\n", i + 1);
-	}
+	ret = gmu_poll_timeout(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT, val,
+		(val & mask) == reset_val, 100, 100000);
 
 	if (ret)
 		DRM_DEV_ERROR(gmu->dev, "GMU firmware initialization timed out\n");
